{
  "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
  "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "John N. Koester, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the course of a drunk driving investigation, quickly securing blood alcohol evidence with as little delay as possible is incredibly important --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How come it took so long for this State to figure out that it needed to do this without a warrant?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John N. Koester, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But in this particular case, it was going to take 90 minutes to two hours to secure the warrant. And during that period of time, the most probative evidence was going to be dissipating, was going to be lost."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Probable cause is not enough. If you have probable cause, then you can get a warrant. But it was and I think still is the main rule that if you can get a warrant, you must do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I think it's quite\nincorrect to say that we -- we don't look at the time\nfactor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Saharsky",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the police officers have to act reasonably in the\nsituation. And in a situation they know for sure the\nevidence is going to be lost, they know that every\nminute is critical."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So is it okay -- is it\nokay to let police officers take the blood?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shapiro",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What Missouri and the United States are\nurging is a categorical exemption to the warrant\nrequirement in all DWI cases nationwide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is this a lot of sound and fury signifying nothing? I mean, what -- what advantage\ndo you think your client would -- would really get from the warrant requirement other than the delay that that would entail allowing his blood alcohol to reduce\nitself?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about that field\nsobriety test? Suppose the person who is apprehended\nand is suspected of being drunk says, I'm not going to\nwalk a straight line. I'm going to just sit here. You\ncan't make me do anything without a warrant.\nDo you need -- if the defendant doesn't\nconsent, do you need a warrant to -- to have the\nstandard sobriety test?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What about a breathalyzer, do you need a warrant for that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Missouri",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Missouri's position is you not only don't need a warrant for a breathalyzer, you don't need a warrant for a blood test."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You have a State trooper here who has been doing this for 17 and a half years. He testifies at the suppression hearing that he has only been required to seek a warrant fewer than ten times."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: So what's the difference between that practical limitation and the limitation that exists in a world -- in a rural jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0002-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the body is continuing to absorb alcohol and then -- and the blood alcohol level is continuing to rise. Only at peak does it then start to dissipate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, I'm sorry, what's the relevance of that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: You don't know when the person's last drink was."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shapiro",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because the process is a very different process. In the typical drug case, which is what this Court has considered when it has examined the question of whether the destruction of evidence qualifies as an exigent circumstance, that question has almost always arisen in what I'll call a typical drug case, Richards v. Wisconsin, Kentucky v. King. And in those situations, what the Court is worried about is that the suspect inside the house is going to flush the drugs down the toilet."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shapiro",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "recognized that even the -- the fingernail scrape was -- was a serious Fourth Amendment issue. Secondly, that evidence, unlike the blood alcohol evidence, was under the control of the defendant and in that case, on the facts of that case, much like many of the Court's other exigent circumstances cases, there was evidence that suggests that the defendant was actively engaged in the process of degrading the evidence at the time that the police stepped in and said we're going to preserve what is left rather than allow you to be the agent of your own destruction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Koester",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "in favor of admittedly less reliable evidence taken at a later time. And I -- that's -- that's simply inconsistent with -- with Fourth Amendment jurisprudence and -- and other destruction of evidence cases. I believe the Respondent's proposed rule here is completely impractical and unworkable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "49b7ed8ba130ca4451e0ae6f0e42868bcf849097d66a2acf0da183ab3a40b18b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-49b7ed8ba130-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2012-11-1425",
      "confidence": 0.0,
